    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Commissions",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4025\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto create a temporary New York state War of 1812 200th anniversary\ncommemoration commission to promote the 200th anniversary of the War of\n1812\n\nPURPOSE OF GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo create a temporary commission to\ncommemorate the 200th anniversary of the War of 1812.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1. Legislative Findings\nSection 2. Creates the commissions; defines terms.\nSection 3. Composition of commission\nSection 4. Powers and duties of the commission.\nSection 5. Assistance to the commission.\nSection 6. Commission authorized to carry out its duties.\nSection 7. Commission will be repealed on December 31, 2015.\nSection 8. Effective Date\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nNew York State played a key role in War of 1812.\nCelebrating this milestone gives New Yorkers the opportunity to\nappreciate and reflect on our rich history. During the years\n2012-2015, New York State will mark, within its borders, the 200th\nanniversary of the great battles of the War of 1812. New York State,\nit's Counties, Cities, Towns and Villages may profit, both culturally\nand economically, from the benefits of a statewide commission to help\norganize, promote and fully implement a major commemoration of the\n200th Anniversary of the War of 1812. By promoting New York State's\nmagnificent history, we can make, New York the ultimate heritage\ntourism destination for the years 2012-2015.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nSame as A.3722\nA.10027B - 2009\nS.6990B - 2009\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNot applicable.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
